NORMETRICS ECONOMETRIC BENCHMARK DEMONSTRATION
============================================================================
Purpose:
To demonstrate that Normetrics reproduces benchmarked classical estimator outputs under aligned specifications and documented numerical tolerances.
Benchmark note:
The examples below are controlled benchmark specifications used to demonstrate estimator reproduction under aligned assumptions. The purpose is numerical reproduction of standard estimators, not substantive inference from a real-world empirical application.
Benchmark families presented:
1. Ordinary Least Squares (OLS)
2. Generalized Least Squares (GLS)
3. Two-Stage Least Squares (2SLS / IV)
Reference implementations:
- statsmodels (OLS, GLS)
- linearmodels.IV2SLS (2SLS / IV)
============================================================================
